<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index rose three points to 1,337.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index rose three points to 1,337.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates rose to 1,337 today from 1,334 on July 2, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1402    12.725	  1394    12.656</p>
<p>   1a   1321 10006.000	  1325 10038.000</p>
<p>   2    1624    23.200	  1602    22.888</p>
<p>   2a   1559 12781.000	  1562 12806.000</p>
<p>   3    1453    13.406	  1442    13.306</p>
<p>   3a   1258  9925.000	  1252  9881.000</p>
